zations and these allow for the  early detection of risk if there's a  problem in the product if a products out  of spec before more work is put into it  you can identify the cause of the issue  and remediated in terms of improving  external relations with customers and  suppliers one of the things that limbs  often have our web portals so that  clients can actually go and look up  their results 24/7 this cuts down time  into  calling the laboratory this also ensures  that the results are posted as soon as  they're available and because there's a  review process in the lens you know that  the results are accurate also it  increases organizational flexibility in  terms of cross-training employees are  happier on the job because they're given  the best tools to do their work and they  don't have to spend time cutting and  pasting results from an instrument onto  an Excel report or a word report and  also it increases organizational data  sharing and it's in a secure database  let's see so many laboratories currently  use outdated limbs or they have paper  and Excel notebooks or they've got  systems that have kind of been cobbled  together with a bunch of homebrew  systems and they're really leaving money  on the table because they're not being  as efficient and productive as they  could we hear many reasons why people  you know move to a newer system their  business needs change and the software  that they purchased five maybe ten years  ago is out you've outgrown it so when  you look at new modern systems some of  the features that you'll see include  very clean user interface the ability to  drag and drop instrument integration is  huge  being able to directly interface the  instruments with the limbs so that in  for some clients their instruments are  modern and they can actually create a  work list in the lens of all the samples  that they're going to run send that to  the instrument the instrument runs all  the samples and then sends back the  results to the limbs without any human  interaction and the nice thing is again  there's no opportunity for transcription  errors the entire fraud process is much  faster and it also results in time and  cost savings another area we talked  about earlier was corrective and  preventative actions so this is very  important in AI so if there's a problem  in the laboratory you can track it you  can track who reported it what actions  were taken to remediated how long it was  open the severity of the issue and who  closed it the nice thing is you have a  record of everything that was done on  that action  another powerful function of a lens is  the ability to do scheduling so if you  have tests that need to be run if you  need to do shelf-life studies those can  also be scheduled if you're talking  about a food product that may be now a  medicinal product so scheduling is very  important there's many things that  computers are very good at and humans  not so much and scheduling is one of  those another aspect is being able to  keep track of all of your instrument  instrumentation in the laboratory in  terms of when it was less calibrated  when it needs to be calibrated being  able to link the manual the electronic  manual to the system so again you have  one secure database that has everything  linked to it in terms of all the  operations of the laboratory rather than  having to run two paper notebooks or  Excel sheets or other systems that were  created internally then also we have the  ability to allow clients to change the  custom captions to terminology that  they're familiar with the advantage of  that this is that it facilitates a rapid  deployment and rapid adoption of new  technology and then also being able to  have a workflow designer allows  laboratories to change the way the  software works to meet their business  rules so with older systems that lack  this function as the clients business  changes or if they move into a new  business they really need to either  customize heavily their software or buy  new software with a workflow designer  you can just change the way that the  software functions in order to leverage  that technology another very powerful  tool is the electronic laboratory  notebook this allows laboratories to go  totally paperless there's many things  that can easily be managed in the limbs  and typically this is called structured  data this is data that's gathered for  example if you're doing a pesticide test  or a microbiology test you're doing the  same test over and over and over  eeehh lens or electronic laboratory  notebooks are good for unstructured data  so if you're doing some R&amp;D or if you  want to test the new compound in  you're only going to do a few tests it's  not really data that a Lim's was  designed to manage but it's perfect for  an electronic lab notebook so you can  basically keep track of experiments that  you've done if there's any inventions if  there's any new compounds in there ideal  for managing this data they also manage  some structure data and they can also  interface with instrumentation in the  laboratory such as balances and pH  meters if we look at the total end  solution because there's so many  different aspects to it you can look at  being able to automatically print  reports being able to access the  software from anywhere with a tablet or  a laptop being able to generate labels I  still see some laboratories where they  manually print labels and I always tell  them that you know when you have a  mistake if someone's dyslexic like I am  and you invert the numbers that mistake  cost you money but if the lens is  already generating the number it really  makes sense to just have the label  printer print that number out there's  also dashboards where you can basically  take a look at the laboratory operations  visually it's very powerful being able  to schedule samples looking at  instrument integration looking at  external storage so that you can store  years and years worth of data being able  to have a web portal that's behind the  firewall where clients can access their  results 24/7 is also very important and  then also having a tool if you're doing  any type of field monitoring or work in  the plant where you can actually enter  results in it captures the GIS  coordinates and then sends that back to  the lens database next we're going to  take a look at some examples of  dashboards if you want to take a look at  the number of samples processed by the  laboratory who the largest client is the  workload capacity you can look at  freezers and refrigerators and  incubators if there's anywhere the  temperature is going below a critical  limit you can have it set up to  automatically send an email or call your  cell phone so there's a lot of tape  capability in these days  boards and each user may have different  things that are important to them so you  can also leverage user specific  dashboards everyone doesn't need to have  the same dashboard as we said before  positive ideas is extremely important it  mitigates errors to make sure that the  numbers that are scanned are accurate  much more accurate than hand entry and  much faster we've talked about one  dimensional bar coding for positive idea  of samples as well as two-dimensional  bar coding you can see in the second  example there's a lot more information  and then there's also RFID radio  frequency which is also becoming very  popular and the nice thing is with all  of these you can actually integrate this  technology with a lot of the  instrumentation to accelerate the  analysis even more so if you have an  analyzer that supports barcodes you can  have all the samples labelled and lined  up in that analyzer and it can read the  barcode generate the result and push it  back to the limbs without any human  intervention too often in the laboratory  we're drowning in data so one of the  major forces is to eliminate as much  paper as possible and with limbs you  have the ability to do that a lot of the  data comes off instruments and if you  don't have to look at printouts and  retype them into lens or push them to  excel and cut and paste them back into  lens you just have the ability to upload  them electronically it's much more  efficient and then also being able to  access that barcodes from anywhere in  the laboratory from sample a sessioning  or log in to final sample disposal you  can create a report of what's ready to  be disposed you can also automatically  generate a certificate of analysis  report as well as invoice reports and  you can also send them to the web portal  so that clients can download those  reports 24/7 and again all this is  reducing the carbon footprint making  sure that a lot lot less papers used we  talked a little previously about  instrument integration we're going to  talk a little bit more now and just  exactly how it works I often have people  ask me while I have an instrument  it's really really old can you still  interface it and the answer is as long  as there's an output file whether it's a  CSV comma separated value and Excel dot  XLS a text XML file new modern  applications are now leveraging Web  Services or you can also talk database  to database but as long as that  instrument has an electronic output file  it can be interfaced and lens  integration is a huge part of any  project that we do today just because  it's one of those places where clients  really get a rapid return on investment  I think we've interfaced over 550  different instruments and the list keeps  growing every day and the beauty of this  is it really makes sure that you have  the highest data quality it eliminates  the possibility of transcription errors  it's much much more accurate and it's  much quicker and in today's world  everyone seems to want everything  yesterday so that is definitely an  advantage the other aspect of lens that  is very nice is the ability to actually  look at the data that you're generating  and understand what it means so you have  the ability to view trends and create  control charts within limbs but many  systems also allow you to integrate with  statistical software so that you can  take a deeper dive into your data one of  the software's that we've integrated  with is JMP by SAS and they actually  have a number of different software  packages for different industries based  on on their needs which are really nice  next we're going to talk about customer  relationship management being able to  give clients the information that  they're looking for in real time and one  way that we can do this is through a web  portal from the lens so as lens manages  samples that are logged in sample  tracking data entry a sample scheduling  QA QC final reporting they show up in  the web portal in real time so once  they've been reviewed and approved in  the lens almost in real time customers  that are on a web portal that secure  can actually see the outcome of that  testing so some testing may already be  completed while other testing might  still be in progress but rather than  calling the laboratory and saying you  know you have my results is my tests  done they are empowered to go to the web  portal and see the results on their own  and if reports are available they can  download them 24/7 and the nice thing is  for the laboratory they have the ability  to see who's logging in who's  downloading reports and many of our  clients also have placed the invoice up  on the web portal so not only can they  download their final analysis report but  then they can also download the final  invoice one of the beauties of the web  portal again is it's available 24/7 but  the other thing is it's a hundred  percent automated from the laboratory  standpoint so once the testing has been  completed it's automatically pushing  this information to the portal there's  no human involved other than the IT  making sure that the server is running  and there's also a much higher level of  customer satisfaction because today's  consumers expect to get their data  electronically and on-demand one of the  biggest benefits is the cost savings  clients laboratories don't need to have  full time client service managers  wasting their time on stuffing envelopes  with final result reports they don't  have to take calls from customers of  past reports that were lost that need to  be resent they don't need to call them  checking the status they have the  ability to check the status themselves  and the fact that there's locked PDFs  that they can print they can print them  out as many times as they want so if  they lose them they can go back to the  state of warehouse and pull the report  they need and reprint it there's also  the ability to do field collection so if  there's large greenhouses and data needs  to be collected this information be can  be collected directly to a tablet the  beauty there is that you don't have  someone filling out a paper form  bringing it back into the laboratory  saying we've had a one or seven because  that data is automatically upload  is once it's entered into the tablet or  the the rugged laptop or the phone  there's a 95 percent reduction in paper  100 percent reduction in the paper  storage cost because all of these  clients that are doing any type of  environmental monitoring that falls into  the EPA they need to hang on to that  paper restore that paper for 10 years  and a 48 percent reduction in cost so  it's a very very smart move for  laboratories that are collecting field  data one of the other areas that people  are investing heavily in is moving their  software solutions to the cloud what  they found is it's very flexible pricing  it's a low cost of entry because they  don't have to manage and maintain the  servers the security that's required the  daily backups and also it's the  deployment is much faster they've really  offshoring their IT a lot of the small  laboratories don't have the funding to  hire a full-time IT administrator  especially when they're starting out and  having software hosted in the cloud is  an ideal alternative standardization  it's all about time savings quality  efficiency and being able to have full  trace pack regulatory compliance is also  very very important but when you  standardize your testing your  terminology it just makes the entire  organization more efficient and more  effective some of the benefits of  automation include having an electronic  chain of custody being able to be in  compliant with many of the regulatory  requirements security is also becoming  more and more important today and then  also being able to keep all of your  instrument calibrations your staff  certifications in one location and  within our system if someone hasn't  completed their training it won't allow  them to put results into the system for  the test they have not been certified on  in the same with instrument if an  instruments out the calibration it won't  let the end user utilize that instrument  for any testing it will tell them  calibrate the instrument or find another  instrument that's within calibration so  things like this that are built into the  zoo  to really enforce quality and compliance  with regulatory requirements we already  talked about the importance of  instrument interfaces being able to  manage inventory and then also being  able to do advanced analytics and  trending in statistics the major  advantage of automation really is  enhanced data quality being able to have  standardization across your organization  whether it's within the United States or  globally and then also cost savings it's  much more cost effective because you're  maximizing your resources by eliminating  mundane tasks that are better left to  computers and not people if we look at  some of the savings of automation 60%  resource savings with result point  client portal 48 percent savings and  these are from different clients and  savings vary by client based on what  their operational procedures are some  people have more room for savings than  others some are very efficient already  and they may see less than others that  are coming from a manual system so 48  percent improvement in lab processing  capabilities 99.9% system availability  for software in the cloud 55 percent  reduction in sample lifecycle processing  time and these are significant savings  on 93 percent reduction in time to  identify out of specification products  so the sooner that you can identify a  problem the sooner you'll be able to  mediate it  so in summary purchasing the right limbs  is very critical for the cannabis  testing laboratory standardization  really does enforce quality and one of  the things that ISO does is it basically  ensures that laboratories have a quality  management system in place so one of the  things that we hear a lot from our  clients is that they want to purchase  software and services from an ISO  certified firm so that they don't have  to do an internal audit on their own  because they know that that's already  been done by another organization making  sure you have the right tool for your  staff is very critical because  laboratories have very highly  brain scientist that our chemist and  microbiologist and they really need the  right tools to do their job if they're  spending time with a calculator checking  formulations by hand they really need to  automate that because one if they're  doing as a calculator each time they do  it they're doing it manually if the  calculation is placed into the lens it's  validated and it's locked it only has to  be done one time and then you know that  from there on forward the lens is going  to be doing it correctly so taking those  mundane tasks away from the end-users  and pushing them to computers really  does make sense the lens also  accelerates in enhances communication  across the organization I know when I  worked in the laboratory and if I was  looking for a sample I was always very  frustrated b