e  laboratory has the number of  customizations if they're currently  using a system that they may need  historical data migration from and if  they have a dedicated project manager  but if they have maybe five instruments  or fewer it could probably be done in  three to four months if they have a  full-time project manager to kind of  take the lead on the project in  laboratories that are new are usually  much faster than laboratories that have  current processes in place that need to  be replaced our next question is can  instruments still be interfaced with the  cloud-based lens yes definitely if  laboratory goes to software as a service  in the cloud model the instrument  integration just occurs a little bit  differently where there's typically a  port in the firewall to allow the data  to be uploaded from the instruments and  we have time for one more question and  this one says what are the benefits of  using an electronic lab notebook if you  have a Lim's the electronic lab notebook  really complements the limbs and that it  captures all the unstructured data that  a limbs typically isn't the best at  managing and maintaining and it really  helps the laboratory to go paperless and  reduce their carbon footprint wonderful  I would like to once again thank dr.  Pascoe for her presentation I would also  like to thank lab rates for making  today's educational webcast possible  before we go I want to let everyone know  that today's webcast will be available  for an on-demand viewing through jun 29  you will receive an email from Roberts  letting you know when this webcast will  be available for replay please share  that announcement with your colleagues  who may have missed today's live event  that's all for now thank you for joining  us  don't be see you again soon goodbye bye
 

